<title>USA: First Empire raises payout, sets buyback.</title>
<headline>First Empire raises payout, sets buyback.</headline>
<dateline>BUFFALO, N.Y. 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Empire State Corp said Wednesday it has raised its quarterly dividend to $0.80 per share from $0.70 per share.</p>
<p>The company also said it plans to buy back up to 303,317 shares of its common stock, or about 4.5 percent of the shares outstanding, and hold it as treasury stock.</p>
<p>The stock repurchased is for use in connection with the possible future exercise of outstanding stock options granted under its 1983 stock option plan, First Empire said.</p>
<p>The shares may be repurchased from time to time in the option market or in privately negotiated transactions, it said.</p>
<p>The dividend is to be paid March 31 to shareholders of record as of the close of business on March 3.</p>
</text>
